<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Granite higher revs seen.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Granite higher revs seen.</headline>
<text>
<p>--Prudential Securities Inc said Monday it raised its 1997 revenue estimate on Granite Broadcasting Corp to $155 million from $135 million to reflect the company's recent acquisition of WXON-TV, a Warner Brothers Network affiliate in Detroit.</p>
<p>--In 1998, Prudential said in a report it looks for the company to have $163 million in net revenues, representing a five percent growth rate.</p>
<p>--Prudential's 18-month price target on the stock is $16.50.</p>
<p>--Granite Broadcasting ended up 1/8 at 10-1/2.</p>
<p>		((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
